  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Star Collection City stands in Mini Blue Heaven and is managed by Combat Beast King. After Fang Yuan annexes too many apertures and the sovereign immortal aperture grows unstable, he arranges Star Collection City as the main city and orders Combat Beast King to oversee overall internal affairs. From there Combat Beast King coordinates reports such as Inkman City in Mini Western Desert and Fire Bird Mountain in Mini Southern Border, and tracks disasters like fire rain from Mini Red Heaven.",
      "chapters": [
        2127
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_mini_blue_heaven",
        "char_combat_beast_king",
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "loc_inkman_city",
        "loc_mini_western_desert",
        "loc_mini_southern_border",
        "loc_mini_red_heaven"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A grand city sits on a continent above cloud soil in Mini Blue Heaven. In its heart is a mountain-like hall made from a star snail. Combat Beast King is appointed Star Collection City Lord by Fang Yuan and oversees aperture internal affairs from that hall. When calamities break out across the aperture, Star Collection City falls into chaos and dispatches manpower and resources to every place.",
      "chapters": [
        2204
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "governance-and-crisis-response",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Twelfth Hair calls Star Collection City the central control area of the sovereign immortal aperture. New arrivals enter it after flying over cloud soil. Originally the Star Collection City Lord was Combat Beast King, but he dies during the tribulation. Afterward Miao Yin, White Rabbit, Wu Shuai, Qi Sea, and other rank eights take turns stationing in Star Collection City. The central square holds three huge pillars whose moving words make up contribution, mission, and exchange boards.",
      "chapters": [
        2241
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "central-control-area",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_twelfth_hair",
        "char_wu_shuai",
        "char_qi_sea_ancestor"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "At Star Collection City Square, Gu Immortals read the contribution board, exchange board, and mission board. Star Collection City is too important to lose, so at least one rank eight Gu Immortal must guard the aperture at all times. Replacement monitoring Gu worms are handed out in Star Collection City, and a sub-hall there restores exhausted Gu Immortals after missions.",
      "chapters": [
        2242
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "three-boards-and-guard-duty",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "sys_gu_worms"
      ]
    }
  ],
